WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:12.059
Today we are going to talk about South Korea,
or as Kim Jong Un would call it, “the bad

00:00:12.059 --> 00:00:15.340
Korea”. You’ve probably heard of this
country because it is where your mobile phone,

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:20.680
or your TV screen, or even your car was manufactured…
Or perhaps because it is the place where the

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:27.599
most watched YouTube video of all time came
from…

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:36.070
Yes, South Korea is a big power: not only
at the cultural level but also at the economic

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:40.670
one. I’m sure everyone of you watching this
video have at least, one product from SAMSUNG,

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.530
HYUNDAI or LG…
&nbsp;

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:48.430
South Korean companies are on fire. And this
is a surprise given that in 1960, South Korea

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:53.490
was an extremely poor country. And no, we
are not talking about relative poverty here.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:59.120
Other countries like Gabon or Zimbabwe were
more developed.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:03.940
&nbsp;
Nonetheless, in just one generation, South

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:08.790
Koreans went from starvation to one of the
most prosperous societies in the world.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.180
&nbsp;
And, so now for the big question: What did

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.820
they do in South Korea to become quite so
rich?

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.190
&nbsp;
Hold on a second though, because I know what

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:20.190
you are thinking if you are a regular viewer…
“Ah, this is just another video where we

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:25.310
explain how a country got marvellously wealthy
thanks to free market capitalism, right?!

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:26.310
RIGHT?!”
&nbsp;

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:33.300
Well, I’m sorry to disappoint you (or not).
But the story of South Korea is a bit different.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:39.500
Of course, compared with their neighbours
to the north, South Korea is a free paradise,

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:45.820
but their economic model has one peculiarity
that sets it apart from the rest of the world…

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:47.600
&nbsp;
So then… What are the reasons that explain

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:53.100
this incredible progress in South Korea? And
more importantly… Why was Gangnam Style

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:59.080
so controversial in South Korea? Both of this
questions are actually related (we promise)

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:04.420
and these are the questions we are going to
answer in this video.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:07.049
FROM THE TOP TO THE BOTTOM
&nbsp;

00:02:07.049 --> 00:02:12.150
As you probably know, in 1953, the Korean
peninsula was split in two halves after a

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:17.280
war in which over 2 million people died. At
that moment we could actually say that South

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.390
Korea was the country that was in more trouble
economically... The North had all the industries

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:26.920
and companies, while the south was agricultural
and underdeveloped region.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:32.120
&nbsp;
Schools had no desks and the most of the children

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:37.260
got the majority of their nutrition from powdered
milk given by the US and Europe. This is why,

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:42.540
in 1960, after many protests, General PARK
CHUN HEE organized a coup d’etat and took

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.870
power in the country. And this is how the
first South Korean dictatorship started.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:49.060
&nbsp;
For the next 27 years the country had 3 different

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:53.410
dictators. And all of them came to power in
a violent way - by overthrowing the previous

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:57.660
dictator. Nonetheless, despite the political
instability, these were the times when the

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.890
South Korean economic model was created.
&nbsp;

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:05.889
But hold on a minute because this economy
is not as free as you might think...

00:03:05.889 --> 00:03:08.280
&nbsp;
In fact, a free market is organized in a bottom

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:13.260
up fashion. The private businesses decide
how, when and what they want to sell. Then,

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:16.730
the state comes in and regulates all that
activity through laws.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:20.680
&nbsp;
Well… PARK CHUN HEE´s system was the opposite.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:25.450
This was a TOP-DOWN system. His policy was
to meet the most important families in the

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:29.980
country, who controlled most of South Korea’s
industries. This group included the founders

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.819
of Samsung and LG.
&nbsp;

00:03:32.819 --> 00:03:38.670
So essentially he put them in a room and said
“Look, from now on, I will give you whatever

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:39.890
you need for you to grow.”
&nbsp;

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:44.319
If one year you cannot pay taxes… it´s
OK! I will forgive you! Do you need some grant?

00:03:44.319 --> 00:03:49.400
Here you have it! Do you need to borrow some
money from abroad? Well the government will

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:54.670
back your loan! Even if you cannot pay your
debts, the state is going to help you!

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:57.890
&nbsp;
“If we are weak,&nbsp;our country&nbsp;will be in

00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:02.379
jeopardy. (…) &nbsp;In order for a country not
to fall, it must cultivate its own strength.”

00:04:02.379 --> 00:04:03.379
--Park Chung Hee
&nbsp;

00:04:03.379 --> 00:04:06.980
Nonetheless, unlike other countries like France,
South Korea didn’t put up any barriers to

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:11.400
international trade. Actually, since that
very first moment, the government guaranteed

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:16.889
rule of law and low taxes for all businesses,
regardless of where did they come from. But

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:21.940
not only that… Park Chun Hee gave all kinds
of tax incentives for companies and individuals

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.850
to invest and save money.
&nbsp;

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:31.970
In other words, the big conglomerates like
HYUNDAI or LOTTE had to compete in an open

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:37.430
market with other corporate juggernauts from
Japan or the US. But, at the same time, they

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:39.020
had the help from the government.
&nbsp;

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:43.710
Since South Korea has no natural resources
but a big population, those companies put

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:49.479
a focus on industries that required a large
workforce: manufacturing.

00:04:49.479 --> 00:04:52.440
&nbsp;
And this was the beginning of…

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:55.910
THE CHAEBOL NATION
&nbsp;

00:04:55.910 --> 00:05:00.610
Imagine the life of one of the 100,000 workers
employed by SAMSUNG in South Korea. He gets

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:05.260
up in the morning in a house built by CyT,
the construction company run by the Samsung

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:08.860
group. While he eats breakfast, he watches
the latest VisualPolitik video (or so we like

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:12.810
to think). He does it from his Samsung Galaxy
phone. Then, he takes his RENAULT-SAMSUNG

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:17.380
car. Yep, you might not know that, but Renault
cars are manufactured by Samsung in South

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:22.350
Korea… And guess where he has his car insurance!
Yep, you’re getting the trend here, he get’s

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:25.169
it from SAMSUNG!
&nbsp;

00:05:25.169 --> 00:05:29.710
Then after a hard day working at… (pause)
yeah, you got it! Now our South Korean man

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:34.350
wants to get some beers with his colleagues.
So he goes to the canteen at… (pause) yep,

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:38.620
you got it! Then, the weekend comes. And our
friend wants to spend some quality time with

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:43.612
his wife and his children. He decides to take
them to a park. Where do you think he will

00:05:43.612 --> 00:05:46.940
go? Yeah, he goes to Samsung’s very own
Disney style theme park…

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:49.710
&nbsp;
In other words, if you work for Samsung, the

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:57.180
company is everything to you. We are talking
about the biggest “CHAEBOL” in all of

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:58.270
South Korea.
&nbsp;

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:02.900
And now you might wonder… What exactly is
a CHAEBOL? Chaebols are those big conglomerates

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:07.229
supported by the state. Some of them, like
the already defunt DAEWOO, were started by

00:06:07.229 --> 00:06:15.000
the administration itself. Others, like HYUNDAI,
were born in the 1940s. All of them started

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:20.210
being family owned but, as they grew, they
became public companies. And all of them have

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:22.180
different business lines...
&nbsp;

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:26.360
For example, LG is famous for their TVs and
their mobile phones... But in South Korea,

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:29.199
they are also the distributors of Coca-Cola.
&nbsp;

00:06:29.199 --> 00:06:34.639
In total, there are around 100 chaebols and
they are the biggest asset in the South Korean

00:06:34.639 --> 00:06:39.120
economy. Now, as I said before, the government
places a red carpet under their feet… but

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.449
this doesn’t mean they have a blank check.
&nbsp;

00:06:41.449 --> 00:06:47.850
This is why when a CHAEBOL as big as DAEWOO
went bankrupt, no one came to bail them out.

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:53.660
And this is is a clear incentive for this
companies to be at the edge of innovation.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:59.449
For instance, in 2008, SONY, the Japanese
firm, wanted to create the first OLED TVs.

00:06:59.449 --> 00:07:03.770
But this technology was not advanced enough
and the screens were pretty expensive, even

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:09.110
priced to high for most of the luxury market.
So the SONY guys put the project on hold,

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.180
and never really got back into it.
&nbsp;

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:19.690
South Korean LG had the same technology and
the same problem. So what did they do? They

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:24.640
launched OLED mobile phones, with a smaller
display. This way, they took advantage of

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:30.100
their assets and, what is more important,
they learned how to work with this new technology.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:34.950
This is why, in a very short amount of time,
they found ways to produce affordable OLED

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:35.950
TV screens.
&nbsp;

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:41.199
But hold on a minute because there is another
important part which helps explain this very

00:07:41.199 --> 00:07:46.069
innovative culture.
SOUTH KOREAN EDUCATION

00:07:46.069 --> 00:07:48.240
&nbsp;
We all know it: South Korean children have

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:53.660
always one of the best marks in the international
PISA test. The whole country stops university

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:58.300
entrance exams start. South Korean schools
spend whatever they need to guarantee the

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:00.740
best education for their boys and girls.
&nbsp;

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:04.870
The flipside of the coin is that those kids
have the biggest child suicide rate in the

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:09.290
world. In fact, all of South Korea has a problem
with suicide -the country having the second

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:12.710
highest suicide rate, per capita, in the world.
&nbsp;

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:18.819
Since the beginning, the government has understood
that CHAEBOLS would need high skilled workers.

00:08:18.819 --> 00:08:25.289
So they designed an educational system that
worked in line with the nation's companies.

00:08:25.289 --> 00:08:29.970
This explains why South Korean children are
incredible good at maths and have excellent

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:31.330
memorisation abilities.
&nbsp;

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:36.860
Further, their respect for authority and hierarchy
is almost religious. And… this is why none

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:40.979
one of them want to start a company. The dream
of every South Korean one is to end up working

00:08:40.979 --> 00:08:45.439
in one of this CHAEBOLS. If they work hard,
they might even become a manager and get a

00:08:45.439 --> 00:08:51.139
house in that paradise on earth, in that famous
district of Seoul with a name that will sound

00:08:51.139 --> 00:08:58.100
familiar to you... Yep, I´m talking about
the GANGNAM DISTRICT.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:05.249
WHAT´S THE MEANING OF GANGNAM STYLE?
&nbsp;

00:09:05.249 --> 00:09:10.259
“A human and warm girl during the day. A
classy one, someone who knows how to enjoy

00:09:10.259 --> 00:09:14.649
the freedom of a cup of coffee but when the
night comes down, her hart gets warmer because

00:09:14.649 --> 00:09:20.699
she is a girl with two faces… Hey, sexy
lady, Opa is Gangnam Style”.

00:09:20.699 --> 00:09:22.610
&nbsp;
This is an extract from that famous song that

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:27.439
became so popular back in 2012. It even lead
to their main singer, PSY, getting into some

00:09:27.439 --> 00:09:31.759
trouble with the authorities due to the lyrics
having “inappropriate content.”

00:09:31.759 --> 00:09:33.489
&nbsp;
For a society that is obsessed with the respect

00:09:33.489 --> 00:09:38.380
for authority, PSY’s aesthetics are something
as radical as the hip movements from Elvis

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:39.399
back in the 50s...
&nbsp;

00:09:39.399 --> 00:09:44.249
But the truth is that a hierarchical economy,
one which relies on a few big corporations

00:09:44.249 --> 00:09:49.269
is not a good recipe for a stable economy.
In fact, South Korea, big as it is in the

00:09:49.269 --> 00:10:01.540
manufacturing industry, lags behind in other
fields such as services or finance. And since

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:06.671
the economy depends so much on governmental
and chaebol decisions, there is almost no

00:10:06.671 --> 00:10:12.029
space for entrepreneurs. Think about it…
even if you want it, it is hard to start a

00:10:12.029 --> 00:10:14.299
company when your competitors are supported
by the government.

00:10:14.299 --> 00:10:17.420
&nbsp;
But not only that! These hierarchical structures

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:22.569
are not as efficient as you might think. In
fact, most of the CHAEBOLS have become bureaucratic

00:10:22.569 --> 00:10:26.180
behemoths that require lots and lots of money
to work. Take Samsung as an example. This

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:31.329
firm leads the sales on mobile phones in the
entire world. However, they make almost no

00:10:31.329 --> 00:10:38.629
profit. And that is a problem.
&nbsp;

00:10:38.629 --> 00:10:42.250
Anyway, things are starting to change. A lot
of South Korean youngsters have been educated

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:47.079
in Europe or America. And now they are coming
back to their country of origin with a new,

00:10:47.079 --> 00:10:52.670
more critical mindset, and a more entrepreneurial
spirit. This new generation is creating the

00:10:52.670 --> 00:11:00.429
roots for an start up ecosystem. But there
is still a lot of work to be done…

00:11:00.429 --> 00:11:03.129
&nbsp;
Anyway, whether you like it or not, we must

00:11:03.129 --> 00:11:08.540
admit that this top-down model has been successful
in South Korea. But despite all of this, there

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:11.339
are still some questions to be answered:
&nbsp;

00:11:11.339 --> 00:11:14.269
What would happen if one day a company like
Samsung collapsed? What would happen to the

00:11:14.269 --> 00:11:18.749
country as a whole? And not only that... This
marriage between politics and business has

00:11:18.749 --> 00:11:23.420
created lots of incentives for corruption
on a massive scale. But that’s something

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:29.929
we are going to cover 
in a future video!

00:11:29.929 --> 00:11:31.420
&nbsp;
